---@class cloudflare.workers.QueryObservabilityTelemetryRequest
---@field account_id string
---@field queryId string Identifier for the query. When parameters are omitted, this ID is used to load a previously saved query's parameters. When providing parameters inline, pass any identifier (e.g. an ad-hoc ID).
---@field timeframe cloudflare.workers.ObservabilityTelemetryQueryRequestTimeframe Timeframe for the query using Unix timestamps in milliseconds. 'from' must be earlier than 'to'. Narrower timeframes produce faster responses and more specific results.
---@field chart? boolean When true, includes time-series data in the response.
---@field chartType? cloudflare.workers.ObservabilityTelemetryQueryRequestChartType|string Controls the SQL shape and response payload for the 'calculations' view. Omitted or 'timeseries_and_aggregate': current behaviour — both the time-series and aggregate queries. 'timeseries': time-series only. 'aggregate': aggregate only. 'distribution': a bucketed 2D histogram (time × value buckets) returned in 'distribution' instead of 'calculations'. 'distribution' is not compatible with 'compare' — combining them returns a 400.
---@field compare? boolean When true, includes a comparison dataset from the previous time period of equal length.
---@field distributionScale? cloudflare.workers.ObservabilityTelemetryQueryRequestDistributionScale|string Value-axis bucketing for chartType 'distribution'. Omitted or 'log': geometric buckets, best for heavy-tailed latency. 'linear': fixed-width buckets, clearer for narrow or additive ranges. Ignored for other chartTypes. The response echoes the scheme used in distribution.bucketMode.
---@field dry? boolean When true, executes the query without persisting the results. Useful for validation or previewing.
---@field granularity? number Number of time-series buckets. Only used when view is 'calculations'. Omit to let the system auto-detect an appropriate granularity.
---@field ignoreSeries? boolean When true, omits time-series data from the response and returns only aggregated values. Reduces response size when series are not needed.
---@field limit? number Maximum number of events to return when view is 'events'. Also controls the number of group-by rows when view is 'calculations'.
---@field offset? string Cursor for pagination in event, trace, invocation, and agent views. Pass the $metadata.id of the last event, the trace cursor, or AgentRun.id to fetch the next page.
---@field offsetBy? number Numeric offset for paginating grouped/pattern results (top-N lists). Use together with limit. Not used by cursor-based pagination.
---@field offsetDirection? string Pagination direction: 'next' for forward, 'prev' for backward.
---@field parameters? cloudflare.workers.ObservabilityTelemetryQueryRequestParameters Query parameters defining what data to retrieve — filters, calculations, group-bys, and ordering. In practice this should always be provided for ad-hoc queries. Only omit when executing a previously saved query by queryId. Use the keys and values endpoints to discover available fields before building filters.
---@field view? cloudflare.workers.ObservabilityTelemetryQueryRequestView|string Controls the shape of the response. 'events': individual log lines matching the query. 'calculations': aggregated metrics (count, avg, p99, etc.) with optional group-by breakdowns and time-series. 'invocations': events grouped by request ID. 'traces': distributed trace summaries. 'agents': agent-specific trace summaries.

---Unwrapped `result` payload of the Cloudflare v4 response envelope.
---@class cloudflare.workers.QueryObservabilityTelemetryResponse
---@field run cloudflare.workers.ObservabilityTelemetryQueryResponseRun Represents a single execution of a query against Workers Observability data, including the query definition, execution status, and performance statistics.
---@field statistics cloudflare.workers.ObservabilityTelemetryQueryResponseStatistics Query performance statistics from the database. Includes execution time, rows scanned, and bytes read. Does not include network latency.
---@field agents? cloudflare.workers.ObservabilityTelemetryQueryResponseAgentsList|distilled.Null Agent run summaries. Present when the query view is 'agents'. Each entry represents one trace containing at least one agent invocation.
---@field calculations? cloudflare.workers.ObservabilityTelemetryQueryResponseCalculationsList|distilled.Null Aggregated calculation results. Present when the query view is 'calculations'. Contains computed metrics (count, avg, p99, etc.) with optional group-by breakdowns and time-series data.
---@field compare? cloudflare.workers.ObservabilityTelemetryQueryResponseCompareList|distilled.Null Comparison calculation results from the previous time period. Present when the compare option is enabled. Same structure as calculations.
---@field distribution? cloudflare.workers.ObservabilityTelemetryQueryResponseDistribution|distilled.Null Bucketed 2D histogram of a numeric field over time. Present when chartType is 'distribution'.
---@field events? cloudflare.workers.ObservabilityTelemetryQueryResponseEvents|distilled.Null Individual event results. Present when the query view is 'events'. Contains the matching log lines and their metadata.
---@field invocations? cloudflare.workers.ObservabilityTelemetryQueryResponseInvocationsMap|distilled.Null Events grouped by invocation (request ID). Present when the query view is 'invocations'. Each key is a request ID mapping to all events from that invocation.
---@field traces? cloudflare.workers.ObservabilityTelemetryQueryResponseTracesList|distilled.Null Trace summaries matching the query. Present when the query view is 'traces'. Each entry represents a distributed trace with its spans, duration, and services involved.

